1287 0 obj
<<
/Title (During the autonomous cutting of tomatoes we often face the problem with the cutting end effector. These systems usually rely on point cloud visual data to identify the cutting point. These points often have discrepancies, leading to inaccuracies in the exact position of the cutting point. This can result in incomplete cuts or damage to the fruit itself.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1278 0 R
/Next 1288 0 R
>>
endobj
1288 0 obj
<<
/Title (Thus we need to have a hook mechanism which pulls out the pedicel from a zone of possibilities of occurrence as per the detected cutting point. Existing tools and automated systems also often lack the capability to securely pull and stabilize the pedicel during cutting, which is crucial for ensuring a clean and precise cut.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1278 0 R
/Prev 1287 0 R
>>
endobj
